{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetry"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.energySlope_eq_convexCap_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.energySlope_eq_convexCap_iff","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.lean#L201-L207","doc":"The same dichotomy at the boundary: `δ` attains the cap exactly when the\ninterface sits *at* the weaker like-species bond (`w = 0`, the pure `σ⁻¹`\ninterface of `BondCutSymmetryLogBound`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.energySlope_gt_convexCap_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.energySlope_gt_convexCap_iff","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.lean#L186-L199","doc":"**The dichotomy: beating the convex cap is exactly leaving the convex hull.**\n`δ > (e_nn - e_pp)/2` **iff** `e_pn > e_nn`, i.e. iff the p–n bond is *weaker\nthan both* like-species bonds. In bond-factor letters (`e = -ln b`, monotone\ndecreasing) that is `b_pn < b_nn ≤ b_pp`: strictly below the convex hull the\ncorpus derives the interface in.\n\nNo sign hypothesis appears, so class B changes nothing about it. The content is\nthat class B does not open a route to the magnitude: an interface outside the\nhull is a *chosen* number, not a derived one, and choosing it to hit `a_A` is a\none-parameter fit (AGENTS.md §NO FITTING, \"selection against the target\"). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.symmetryCoeff_le_of_energySlope_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.symmetryCoeff_le_of_energySlope_le","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.lean#L175-L184","doc":"**Monotonicity of the symmetry coefficient in the slope.** Any bound on `δ`\ntransports to a bound on `a_A^eff` with no sign hypothesis on the energies; this\nis the bridge the archimedean sibling uses to compose the `2 ln q` cap into a\nMeV cap for class B. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.enn_neg_of_semf_neutronMatter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.enn_neg_of_semf_neutronMatter","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.lean#L153-L173","doc":"**Class B's escape has a price: a repulsive neutron–neutron bond.** If a\npair-additive bond count reproduces the SEMF at pure neutron matter — where the\nSEMF with `a_A > a_V` is negative, i.e. unbound — then the n–n energy is\nstrictly negative. In bond-factor letters `e_nn = -ln b_nn < 0` means\n`b_nn > 1`.\n\nThis is the honest statement of what dropping `bondSum_nonneg` costs: the escape\nis real, and it converts a *structural* exclusion into a *falsifiable condition\non a derived quantity*. The hypothesis `a_V < a_A` is what AME2020 measures; it\nenters here as a hypothesis, never as a fit. Conditional-lemma naming per\nAGENTS.md §Conditional-proved ≠ premise-established. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.bondSum_neutronMatter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.bondSum_neutronMatter","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.lean#L145-L151","doc":"**The bond sum at pure neutron matter is `e_nn · n_nn`.** With `Z = 0` there\nare no p–p and no p–n bonds; this is the composition at which `bondSum_nonneg`\ndid its work. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.bondSum_wellMixed_energyShift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.bondSum_wellMixed_energyShift","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.lean#L124-L134","doc":"**A uniform energy shift on the well-mixed layout is a pure volume term.**\nIt adds `s·k·A/2` — linear in `A = Z + N`, with no `(N-Z)²` and no dependence on\nthe mixing density `μ`. Combined with `symmetryCoeff_energyShift`, the shifted\nlaw's symmetry coefficient is the unshifted one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.bondSum_wellMixed_totalCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.bondSum_wellMixed_totalCount","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.lean#L117-L122","doc":"**The well-mixed layout has total bond count `kA/2`, independently of the\nmixing density.** The `μ·Z·N` bonds the mixing creates are taken from the\nlike-species counts one for one, so `μ` cancels. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.symmetryCoeff_energyShift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.symmetryCoeff_energyShift","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.lean#L110-L115","doc":"The symmetry coefficient inherits the shift-invariance, for every mixing\ndensity `μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.energySlope_energyShift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.energySlope_energyShift","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.lean#L101-L108","doc":"**The p–n slope is invariant under a uniform energy shift.** `δ` is a\nsecond difference of the three energies, so a common additive constant cancels\nidentically. This is the whole of class B's uniform sub-case in one line: making\nevery bond repulsive at once changes `δ` by exactly zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.bondSum_energyShift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.bondSum_energyShift","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite.lean#L82-L91","doc":"**A uniform shift of all three bond energies adds the shift times the total\nbond count.** In bond-factor letters `e = -ln b`, a shift by `s` is the common\nrescaling `b_t ↦ e^{-s}·b_t`; taking `s` negative enough drives every energy\nbelow zero, which is exactly class B. What it buys is a term proportional to\n`n_pp + n_pn + n_nn`, and nothing else. ","signatureChunk":0}]}